  "description": "A windtrap draws water from the exposed desert air. Its output becomes physical rations that colonists can haul to cisterns, workshops and travel stores.\n\nAn established group of collectors reduces dependence on carried supplies, but their usefulness depends on siting and access. Leave space for intakes and for workers hauling the finished water.",
