    "overview": {
      "body": "Windtraps provide the regular water supply for a growing settlement. Their harvest supports drinking, irrigation and water-fed cooling, so expansion places new demands on collection even before another colonist arrives."
    },
    "settlementRole": {
      "body": "Keep a reserve between collector output and daily demand. A cistern protects stored rations, while sensible hauling routes keep that reserve available to beds, growers and thirsty colonists."
    },
    "siting": {
      "body": "Unroofed air and unobstructed space around the collector improve capture. Nearby walls and roofs restrict the intake; a sealed intake stops collection. Check the building’s environmental efficiency when placing it near a cliff or courtyard wall."
    },
